# ios/tools/audit-binary.allowlist: exact exceptions for ios/tools/audit-binary.sh.
#
# Format: <object-label> <symbol> <reason...>, separated by whitespace.
# - object-label is the label the audit prints: the path relative to the parent
#   directory of the argument, with <path>(<member>) for an archive member.
# - symbol is the exact imported symbol, or <Name>.framework for a framework
#   finding.
# - Both must equal a finding exactly. Entries are never patterns or prefixes.
# - A line with fewer than 3 fields stops the audit (exit 2).
#
# Rules (mirror plan, spike 3c):
# - Never allowlist anything in our own objects: CoreCrypto.o, SsaPdf.o,
#   NetCanary.o, SsaCore.framework.o (our Kotlin), or NetworkGuardTests.xctest.
#   A hit in our own Swift or Kotlin is a defect to fix, not an exception.
# - Never weaken a pattern in the script to make an entry unnecessary.
# - Each identical symbol in each object gets its own line: the two XCFramework
#   slices and each test bundle are separate objects.
#
# How the reasons were traced (Run 7, 2026-11-23, Xcode 27.2, Kotlin 2.0.21):
# - `xcrun nm -A -U` on each slice's SsaCore archive: every platform-cache hit
#   below has a cinterop binding `_platform_<lib>_<name>_wrapper<N>` defined in
#   the same member. The caches define 1674 (simulator) / 1677 (device) posix,
#   1103 CoreFoundation and 742 Foundation wrappers, far more than core uses.
# - `xcrun nm -u -A` on the archive: SsaCore.framework.o, our compiled Kotlin,
#   references the platform libraries only through their __Konan_init_*
#   initialisers and knifunptr_platform_CoreCrypto32_CC_SHA256; no networking
#   or dynamic-lookup binding.
# - Archive members are not linked, so nm cannot show a bound library for them.
#   In the linked test bundles, every one of these platform-cache imports is
#   gone except _dlsym, which `xcrun nm -m` shows as `(from libSystem)`.

# -- SsaCore.xcframework: Kotlin/Native platform interop caches (audit a) ------
SsaCore.xcframework/ios-arm64-simulator/SsaCore.framework/SsaCore(liborg.jetbrains.kotlin.native.platform.posix-cache.a.o) _connect Kotlin/Native prebuilt platform.posix interop cache defines the binding _platform_posix_connect_wrapper528; our Kotlin (SsaCore.framework.o) references no such binding
