# -- SsaCore.xcframework built by :ui: Compose, Skia and Kotlin 2.4.21 (audit a) -
# Owner decision, 2026-11-28 (the iOS MVP's D1). Since the iOS MVP, :ui builds this framework
# with Compose Multiplatform 1.12.2 (Skiko) and Kotlin 2.4.21 inside it. Traced on each member
# with `ar -x`, then `xcrun objdump -d -r` for the calling function and `strings` for what it
# looks up. None of these members names a networking framework, class or symbol:
# - CMPLayoutRegion.o (Compose): -[CMPLayoutRegion edgeInsetsForLayoutRegionInView:] calls
#   NSClassFromString("UIViewLayoutRegion"), a UIKit class that only newer iOS versions have;
# - libskia.SkCTFont.o: SkCTFontGetNSFontWeightMapping looks up the nine UIFontWeight* constants;
# - fontmgr_mac_ct.SkFontMgr_mac_ct.o: the SkFontMgr_Mac constructor looks up
#   CTFontManagerCopyAvailableFontFamilyNames;
# - fontmgr_mac_ct.SkTypeface_mac_ct.o: SkTypeface_Mac::onGetVariationDesignParameters looks up
#   kCTFontVariationAxisHiddenKey;
# - libskia_ganesh_ext.GrGLMakeNativeInterface_iOS.o: GrGLInterfaces::MakeIOS dlopens the system
#   GL library and looks up OpenGL ES functions in it;
# - libkotlin.native.internal.4fyzlt.a.o, simulator slice only: the Kotlin runtime's
#   TryInitializeCoreSymbolication (12 call sites), stack-trace symbolication through
#   CoreSymbolication.framework. With Kotlin 2.4.21 this replaces the Kotlin 2.0.21 entry for
#   libstdlib-cache.a.o (_Kotlin_getSourceInfo_core_symbolication, 11 call sites), which matched
#   nothing after the upgrade and was removed by owner decision on 2026-11-28. The member name
#   carries a hash and may change with Kotlin.
