# -- :models iOS simulator test executable (Run 8 Step 6, spike 3b) ------------
# android/models/build/bin/iosSimulatorArm64/debugTest/test.kexe, the first linked image with
# ONNX Runtime inside, audited by passing that file, so its label is test.kexe. `xcrun nm -m`
# binds _dlsym (from libSystem); `xcrun otool -tvV` puts its 22 call sites in ONNX Runtime's
# onnxruntime::(anonymous)::PosixEnv::GetSymbolFromLibrary (1), Kotlin/Native's
# _Kotlin_getSourceInfo_core_symbolication (11), and clang compiler-rt's availability check
# __initializeAvailabilityCheck (10: dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, ...) of CoreFoundation functions),
# linked in for ___isPlatformVersionAtLeast, which ONNX Runtime's prelinked_objects.o imports.
# The compiler-rt caller was not expected by the Run 8 plan; the owner confirmed the entry on
# 2026-11-28. The same compiler-rt function is the caller allowlisted in the iOS app's images.
test.kexe _dlsym from libSystem; callers in the linked :models test executable are ONNX Runtime 1.22.0's onnxruntime::(anonymous)::PosixEnv::GetSymbolFromLibrary, Kotlin/Native's _Kotlin_getSourceInfo_core_symbolication, and clang compiler-rt's __initializeAvailabilityCheck (pulled in by ONNX Runtime's ___isPlatformVersionAtLeast references), traced with otool -tvV; not our Kotlin

# -- The iOS app, SsaAssistant.app (the iOS MVP's D1) ----------------------------
# Owner decision, 2026-11-28. tests/ios-audit.js audits every top-level entry of the built
# SsaAssistant.app except PlugIns/, so these labels are paths inside the .app. PlugIns/ holds
# the test bundle that `xcodebuild test` embeds; an installed app has none. That bundle,
# SsaAssistantTests.xctest, gets no entry: its NetworkTrapTests calls URLSession on purpose,
# and tests/ios-audit.js checks that it FAILS the audit, naming NSURLSession.
# These are linked images, so one entry covers every caller of the symbol in the image.
# tests/ios-audit.js therefore also checks, with `xcrun otool -tvV`, that the functions
# referencing _dlsym and _NSClassFromString in each image are exactly the ones named below:
# a new caller, ours or a library's, fails the test until it is traced and added here.
# - SsaAssistant: Xcode's debug-dylib launcher stub (ENABLE_DEBUG_DYLIB, Debug builds only);
#   _getDebugDylibEntryPoint and its _OUTLINED_FUNCTION_34 look up the app's entry point in
#   SsaAssistant.debug.dylib. Our Swift is not in this file.
# - SsaAssistant.debug.dylib (our Swift shell): the only caller is clang compiler-rt's
#   __initializeAvailabilityCheck (10 call sites), linked in for Swift's #available checks.
# - SsaKit_1BC8669A2A8895_PackageProduct (the package's one product, with SsaCore, Compose,
#   Skia and ONNX Runtime linked in): the Compose, Skia and Kotlin callers traced in the
#   SsaCore section above, ONNX Runtime's PosixEnv::GetSymbolFromLibrary (see its section),
#   and compiler-rt's __initializeAvailabilityCheck. The hash in the name comes from Xcode;
#   if it changes, these labels must follow it.
SsaAssistant _dlsym from libSystem; Xcode's debug-dylib launcher stub (_getDebugDylibEntryPoint) looks up the entry point in SsaAssistant.debug.dylib; Debug builds only; not our code
SsaAssistant.debug.dylib _dlsym from libSystem; the only caller is clang compiler-rt's __initializeAvailabilityCheck (Swift #available), traced with otool -tvV; not our Swift
Frameworks/SsaKit_1BC8669A2A8895_PackageProduct.framework/SsaKit_1BC8669A2A8895_PackageProduct _dlsym from libSystem; callers are Skia's font and GL setup, Kotlin/Native's TryInitializeCoreSymbolication, ONNX Runtime's PosixEnv::GetSymbolFromLibrary and compiler-rt's __initializeAvailabilityCheck, traced with otool -tvV and pinned by tests/ios-audit.js; not our code
Frameworks/SsaKit_1BC8669A2A8895_PackageProduct.framework/SsaKit_1BC8669A2A8895_PackageProduct _NSClassFromString from Foundation; the only caller is Compose's -[CMPLayoutRegion edgeInsetsForLayoutRegionInView:] (UIViewLayoutRegion), traced with otool -tvV and pinned by tests/ios-audit.js; not our code
